The primary-source check supports the central model: `direct-tcpip` is accepted and connected on the server side after privilege drop; SOCKS5 is `CONNECT`-only; macOS sshuttle uses PF and supports TCP plus DNS, not general UDP. I also found one audit detail to keep watching: the local OpenSSH checkout is shallow `master`, while the document’s links are correctly pinned to `V_10_2_P1`; I’m validating the pinned tag directly so the verdict does not rely on the checkout label.
